NASA Anomaly detection - Dockerized ML Project

Overview
This project implements anomaly detection on NASA turbofan engine degradation simulation data using Isolation Forest algorithm. This algorithm was chosen as it is good for high dimensional data without the assumption of normal distribution and is unsupervised The pipeline is containerized with Docker.

The model is trained with data and the plots to show anomalies prediction results on test and train data written into CSV output files are saved inside the container. 

Main Features
    Anomaly detection with Isolation forest
    Prometheus metrics : Anomaly count, CPU, Memory percentage
    Grafana dashboards : real time anomaly visualization
    Dockerize setup with multiple containers
    Logging module to log anomalies

Project Structure
nasa-anomaly/
|----CMAPSS_IsolationForest.py
|----DataReadme.txt
|----Dockerfile 
|----README
|----requirements.txt
|----test_FD001.txt
|----train_FD001.txt
|----docker-compose yml
|----prometheus.yml
|----grafana/

* Dockerfile
    Defines the container environment using python:3.9-slim as the base image.
        The Dockerfile has comments included for every execution

* requirements.txt list all dependencies in PyPI version only

* train_FD001.txt   
    Holds the training data

* test_FD001.txt
    Hold the test data

* DataReadme
    Information on training and test data

* CMAPSS_IsolationForest.py
    ML script to train the model and classify the data points

* docker-compose.yml
    Sets up a multi-container environment with all services networked

* prometheus.yml
    Configuration for prometheus


Folder structure generated after runtime 
|----output/
    |----TestAnomalyResults
    |----TrainAnomalyResults
    |----plot/
        |----anomaly_plot*.png
    |----Anomaly.log 

*output
    *TestAnomalyResults
        Anomalies predicted in test data
    *TrainAnomalyResults
        Anomalies predicted in train data
    *plots/
        Plots with anomalies and correct data points


PROJECT WORKFLOW
*   # In the terminal, inside the folder, Clones the repository
    git clone http://github.com/BhatPrithvi/nasa-anomaly.git     
    cd nasa-anomaly

    docker-compose up --build 
    # Runs the file docker-compose .This will start three services
    #    * ML container (nasa-ml)
    #           Runs python script, exposes Prometheus metrics on port 8000
    #           http://localhost:8000  -> raw metrics text
    #    * Prometheus container
    #           Scraps(reads) metrics from nasa-ml:8000/metrics
    #           http://localhost:9090  -> Prometheus UI (Targets, Graph, etc.)
    #    * Grafana container
    #           Grafana dashboards query Prometheus which has data scraped from Prometheus container and visualizes data on dashboard
    #           http://localhost:3000  -> Grafana UI( default : admin/admin)

*   Grafana configuration
    1. Open Grafana --> Add Data Source --> choose Prometheus
    2. Set URL : http://prometheus:9090
    3. Create a dashboard

* ML Script overview
    * Isolation forest used to detect anomalies
    * Log files generated
    * Exposes Prometheus gauges  

*   Logs, Output and Monitoring
    * All plots and predictions logged to the output/ folder
    * Prometheus scraps metrics every 5 seconds
    * Grafana dashboards visualize metrics in real time


# Grafana Dashboard

The project includes a pre-configured Grafana dashboard in the folder grafana/dashboard.json for visualization

# Steps :

1. Open Grafana at [http://localhost:3000] and log in (default: admin/admin)
2. Click the **“+” → Import** button
3. Either:
   - Upload the JSON file: `grafana/dashboard.json` (included in this repo), or
   - Copy-paste the JSON content into the import textbox
4. Select the Prometheus datasource (default: `Prometheus`) and click **Import**
5. The dashboard will display:
   - Metrics defined in ML container
